Sebastian Kaiser, not a separate entity inferred from a project name.

The entire sdk/go/ subtree as distributed by Licensor, including its worker
client, handlers, protocol schemas and generated bindings, is separately
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 in sdk/go/LICENSE. It is
excluded from the Licensed Work. Separately licensed third-party materials
and materials carrying their own license notices are also excluded to the
extent of those separate licenses. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and the
applicable notices accompanying those materials.

No provision of this License imposes additional conditions on rights validly
granted under those separate licenses, including conditions concerning AI,
patents, contributions, public forks, commercial use, redistribution, or
termination. Those rights remain subject to their own license terms.

Using, modifying, distributing or selling the Apache-licensed SDK, software
using that SDK, or an independent implementation of its public interfaces
does not by itself require an engine commercial license. You may license
Your own independent worker or application code under terms of Your choice.
The SDK portions retain their Apache License terms. Incorporating or
supplying engine code, including an engine-licensed adapter, remains subject
to the terms applicable to that engine code.

Combining materials in one file, binary, package, container or repository
does not eliminate the licenses governing their respective portions. Moving
engine material into sdk/go/, or moving separately licensed material out of
that subtree, does not by itself change its license. Inclusion in a
