2. Definitions

"Licensor" means Sebastian Kaiser, acting as the holder of or person
authorized to license the rights granted under this License.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
License.

"Your Company" means You and any legal entity that You control, that
controls You, or that is under common control with You. "Control" means
direct or indirect ownership of more than fifty percent of the voting
interests, or the legal power to direct management and policies.

"Service Provider" means a contractor, consultant, cloud provider, hosting
provider, CI/CD provider, security reviewer, AI tool provider, or other third
party acting on behalf of and under the direction of Your Company solely
for the activities permitted to Your Company under this License. A provider
may serve multiple customers; each engagement must independently meet the
conditions of this License. Providing an Engine Offering on the provider's
own account is not acting as a Service Provider for that offering.

"Permitted Internal Use" means use of the Licensed Work under Your
Company's control for Your Company's own business operations. It includes
development, testing, CI/CD, QA, evaluation, benchmarking, security and
compliance review, staging, and production. Personal study and
noncommercial experimentation are also permitted, subject to the same
conditions on distribution and provision of engine capabilities to others.

Permitted Internal Use includes operating the engine as a backend component
of Your Company's own products and services, including paid products and
services, when customers receive application-specific business operations
and their results rather than an Engine Offering. Examples include order
processing, device polling, maintenance, and generation and delivery of
customer reports. Earning revenue from those applications does not by
itself require a commercial license.

Customers may select, parameterize, schedule, repeat, or combine operations
defined by Your application where that configuration remains confined to
the application's business functions. Choosing a report's contents,
delivery time, recurrence or recipients does not by itself create an Engine
Offering. This permission does not extend to an application that supplies
general execution or orchestration capability under a domain label or
through a thin wrapper.

Your Company must retain authority over the purpose and permitted scope of
its use, including work performed on its behalf by Service Providers. A
provider's ownership of infrastructure does not by itself prevent Permitted
Internal Use. Customer-specific accounts or dedicated instances do not by
themselves convert a provider's Engine Offering into a qualifying service
engagement. Shipping or otherwise supplying engine code to customers of
Your product remains subject to Sections 5 and 12, except for the limited
private service engagements and contribution activities expressly allowed
by Sections 3 and 7.

"Engine Functionality" means the capabilities supplied by operating or
incorporating the Licensed Work or its modifications to accept, schedule,
coordinate, dispatch or execute jobs; maintain durable runs, conversations,
events, timers and action outcomes; manage workers, execution resources,
leases and worker releases; operate replicated controller clusters; or
administer, monitor and recover those facilities. This term describes the
capabilities of the Licensed Work and does not assert exclusive rights in
functionality, ideas, principles, algorithms, interfaces or facts.

"Engine Offering" means using, operating, providing or incorporating the
Licensed Work or its modifications to supply Engine Functionality to third
parties as an execution engine, job queue, scheduler, orchestration
platform, worker platform or similar infrastructure capability, whether
hosted, managed, embedded, white-labelled or exposed through a wrapper, and
whether paid or free. It includes permitting customers to submit or
configure general-purpose jobs or workflows, execute customer-supplied
programs as general computing tasks, or register or manage workers for
their own execution purposes through the engine. The capability actually
supplied determines this classification; branding, a nominal application
domain, a separate customer license, or single tenancy is not sufficient
to make an Engine Offering Permitted Internal Use. Application configuration
expressly permitted above and qualifying Service Provider work under
Section 3 are excluded. Independent software and the Apache-licensed SDK
are excluded as stated in the scope provisions and Section 5.

"Commercial Redistribution" means selling, renting, leasing, sublicensing,
publishing, distributing or otherwise supplying the Licensed Work in
source or object form to a third party for payment or commercial advantage.
Noncommercial distribution is separately addressed in Section 5(b).

"Product Embedding" means including, bundling, integrating, linking,
packaging, containerizing or shipping the Licensed Work as part of a
product, appliance, developer tool or other offering supplied to a third
party, or incorporating it into an Engine Offering. Operating the internal
backend of an application within Permitted Internal Use is excluded.

"Engine Expression" means copyright-protected expression in the Licensed
Work, including protected source or object code and protected portions of
documentation, examples, tests, fixtures, templates, scripts and other
materials. It does not include unprotected ideas, principles, algorithms,
functionality, facts, or interface and format concepts merely as such, nor
materials excluded from this License by the scope provisions. Whether
expression is protected is determined by applicable law.

"AI System" means a machine learning, foundation, language, code-generation,
embedding, classification, recommendation or other artificial intelligence
system, including an automated software engineering or agentic system.

"AI Training Use" means using material forming part of the Licensed Work
as training, adaptation, evaluation or model-development content for an AI
System, including:

(a) pre-training, training, fine-tuning, retraining, distilling or adapting
    model parameters or learned behavior using that material;

(b) creating, augmenting, curating, labeling, testing or supplying training,
    preference, evaluation, red-team or benchmark datasets using that
    material for the development, selection or improvement of an AI System;

(c) generating synthetic data from that material for the purposes in
    paragraphs (a) or (b); or

(d) retaining or incorporating that material in reusable model-development
    corpora or services for those purposes outside the particular assistance
    permitted by Section 6.

This definition applies to repository history, issues, discussions, comments
and metadata only to the extent they form part of the Licensed Work and
Licensor has the rights necessary to govern that use. It excludes permitted
private AI assistance under Section 6, including its private retrieval and
indexing. It also excludes operating Duravela to orchestrate AI or ML
workloads using Your Materials or other materials You are entitled to use,
without supplying the Licensed Work as model-development content. Testing
the engine or a proposed patch with an AI-assisted tool is not, by itself,
evaluation of the AI System for the purposes of this definition.

"Your Materials" means Your software, configuration, tests, data,
documentation and other materials, to the extent they do not contain Engine
Expression copied or adapted from the Licensed Work. Merely interacting
with the engine, implementing an interface, or embodying an unprotected
idea does not make material Engine Expression.

"Output" means a job result, action result, report, log, artifact, event,
generated file or other output produced by running the Licensed Work.

"Engine Contribution" means code, documentation or other material You
intentionally submit to Licensor for inclusion in the Licensed Work and
have authority to license. It excludes contributions to the Apache-licensed
SDK or other separately licensed material, and communications clearly
identified when submitted as not offered for inclusion. Material retains
its existing rights if it is merely attached to illustrate a problem and
is clearly identified as not offered for inclusion.

