6. AI assistance, model development and text-and-data mining

6.1 Restricted model-development use

This License grants no permission for AI Training Use. Subject to Section 1
and any separate applicable rights, AI Training Use requires a separate
written license from Licensor. You may not supply the Licensed Work to a
provider on terms permitting that provider to use it for AI Training Use
unless that use is independently authorized.

6.2 Permitted private assistance

You may use local or third-party AI-assisted tools to inspect, explain,
summarize, search, privately index or embed, debug, modify, document, test
or review the Licensed Work, including for security review, solely for
Permitted Internal Use or the contribution activities in Section 7,
provided that:

(a) the Licensed Work and Engine Expression in prompts, private indexes
    and generated material are not used for AI Training Use;

(b) access is confined to You, authorized participants in that work, and
    providers processing the material on Your behalf under contractual
    or effective technical restrictions that prevent their independent
    training, model improvement, dataset creation or reuse for other
    customers;

(c) provider retention is limited to processing necessary for the requested
    assistance or storage solely for Your private account, tenant or
    deployment, including its controlled backups, subject to the same
    restrictions on access and reuse; and

(d) Engine Expression is disclosed or distributed only through the private
    access permitted by Section 3 or the contribution workflow in
    Section 7.

Confidential processing by a provider meeting these conditions is permitted
disclosure, not prohibited redistribution. A provider acting for this
purpose receives the limited direct permission in Section 3. Private
retrieval, embeddings, inference, code completion and generation of fixes
or tests under this subsection are not AI Training Use. The exception
does not permit fine-tuning or other model-development use of engine
materials merely because the model or deployment is private.

An AI-assisted change may be submitted and displayed through an authorized
contribution fork or pull request under Section 7. You remain responsible
for having the rights necessary to submit it. This subsection grants no
additional rights to operate an Engine Offering or publish engine code.

6.3 Workloads and separate materials

You may use Duravela for otherwise permitted AI or ML workloads, including
scheduling training, evaluation and inference jobs, using Your Materials
or other materials You are entitled to use. Running those jobs does not
constitute AI Training Use of Duravela merely because Duravela executes or
coordinates them. The engine's protected materials must not be supplied as
model-development content without applicable permission. Ordinary factual
Outputs remain governed by Section 4, and the SDK remains governed solely
by its Apache License and applicable separate notices.

6.4 Reservation and independent rights

For purposes of Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790, Section 44b(3) of
the German Copyright Act, and analogous provisions that permit a rights
reservation, Licensor reserves text-and-data-mining and AI Training Use
rights in the Licensed Work to the extent those rights may lawfully be
reserved. This reservation excludes activities expressly permitted by this
License and does not restrict mandatory exceptions or separately granted
rights. Its effect is subject to applicable requirements, including any
requirement for a machine-readable reservation for online materials.

This License does not revoke or amend a separate permission validly granted
by the relevant rights holder to a repository host, platform or other
party. No additional AI-training permission is granted by the public-fork
permission in Section 7. Neither this paragraph nor a reference to a
hosting service is a representation about the terms of any separate
