14. Breach, cure and termination

14.1 Non-deliberate curable breaches

For a non-deliberate breach of this License that is capable of remedy
and is not a repeated breach covered by Section 14.2, You have thirty
(30) days to remedy the breach after You become aware of it or receive
notice identifying it, whichever occurs first. Your otherwise permitted
rights remain in effect during that period. You must promptly stop the
noncompliant activity and begin corrective action without undue delay.
Compliant internal operations may continue during that period.
The cure opportunity is not excluded solely because the breach concerns
distribution, embedding, an Engine Offering, AI use or notices.

During cure, You may not continue the prohibited activity, expand the
unauthorized distribution or offering, or make further unauthorized
disclosures. Corrective action includes restoring missing notices,
ending unauthorized access or availability under Your control, and
taking reasonable steps to request removal of unauthorized copies from
recipients. Cure does not require a representation that already disclosed
information can be made unknown. Whether an irreversible use can be
remedied depends on its circumstances; written agreement with Licensor
may be required where full remedy is not possible.

If You fully remedy the breach within that period, Your rights continue
without interruption. Otherwise, the rights granted under this License
terminate at the end of the thirty-day period. If You fail to stop the
noncompliant activity promptly or begin corrective action without undue
delay, Licensor may terminate by notice before that period ends, subject
to mandatory law. Licensor may agree in writing to additional time or a
specified remedy.

14.2 Other breaches

For a deliberate breach, repetition of substantially the same breach
after a previous cure under Section 14.1, or a breach not capable of
remedy, Licensor may terminate this License by notice stating the grounds,
subject to any mandatory notice, warning or cure requirements. Nothing
permits prohibited use while a termination notice is pending. Mandatory
rights to terminate for serious cause and remedies concerning unauthorized
activity remain unaffected. Patent termination is governed separately by
Section 9.

14.3 Consequences and surviving rights

After termination, You must stop activities requiring this License and
delete or destroy copies held solely under it, including modified builds,
except copies retained for legal, evidentiary or bona fide archival backup
purposes. Retained copies may not be restored or used for engine operation
without applicable permission. Reasonable ordinary backup-retention cycles
may be used for inaccessible archival copies.

Termination does not require destruction of Your Materials, factual
Outputs or separately licensed material and does not terminate independent
rights in those materials. Section 4 and valid contribution grants under
Section 7 survive. Provisions concerning retained rights, accrued claims,
warranty, liability and disputes survive to the extent relevant to their
purpose. Cure preserves the license where stated; it does not waive claims
arising from the breach. Reinstatement after termination requires Licensor's
written consent unless mandatory law provides otherwise.

